    "prose": "Rain hammered above the workshop and swept past the wide gate in slanting sheets. Aya held her side of the restored mosaic level. Across from her, Mert kept his side steady.\n\n“Ready?” he asked.\n\nAya felt the old urge to answer by stepping out first and making him catch up. The fragile panel between them stopped her. “Ready. You set the pace.”\n\nMert began a slow count. “One step. Then another.”\n\nAya moved through the wide workshop gate into the covered yard. She stopped before her arms could pull ahead.\n\nMert moved through the wide workshop gate into the covered yard. He kept his shoulders square to hers.\n\nThe mosaic panel moved through the wide workshop gate into the covered yard between them. Their shared hold remained stable, and the restored surface stayed intact.\n\nWind drove rain beyond the covered route, loud enough to make the yard seem smaller. Aya’s first instinct was to hurry away from the noise. She tightened her attention instead of her grip.\n\nMert took one careful step.\n\nAya matched that step exactly.\n\nHe took another, no faster than before. Aya matched his pace again, keeping her side level rather than trying to lead the shared carry.\n\nMert watched her feet, then looked across the panel at her. He had seen that she was no longer surging ahead.\n\n“That’s steady,” he said.\n\nAya gave a short nod. Praise from him still felt strange, but not unwelcome. “Then steady is how we keep going.”\n\nThey paused together in the covered yard, still holding the same intact panel between them. Rain beat harder outside their shelter, but neither of them rushed toward the ramp.",
